%R	2730069	83219402	106343	237851	<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN""><HTML><HEAD><META content=""text/html; charset=unicode""http-equiv=Content-Type><META name=HENERATOR content=""MSHTML 11.00.10570.1011""></HEAD><BODY><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-02 12:37: Fibrebond Delivery date is 12/18. Due to the coordination and/or the other building ROJ dates impacting DC1 ROJs, this has been pushed out. Fibrebond can only deliver so many a week and all building need by dates overlap.</P></BODY></HTML>
%R	2730070	83219401	106343	237851	<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN""><HTML><HEAD><META content=""text/html; charset=unicode""http-equiv=Content-Type><META name=HENERATOR content=""MSHTML 11.00.10570.1011""></HEAD><BODY><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-02 12:37: Fibrebond Delivery date is 12/22. Due to the coordination and/or the other building ROJ dates impacting DC1 ROJs, this has been pushed out. Fibrebond can only deliver so many a week and all building need by dates overlap.</P><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-30 08:24: Per Trucking/Delivery Company: This POD is now tentatively set to be delivered on 1/2/2026.<br>Updates/History:<br>12/30: Truck broke down/in shop for repair. (details below)<br>Per Trucking/Delivery Company Our driver Perry is experiencing a D-Rating issue with the truck this am and does not have power.  He is currently in a shop, but this will not allow us to meet our police this am to get on site this afternoon.  I truly apologize for this!  The goal is to get out of the shop today and we are working on police scheduling for tomorrow.  I am curious what the sites schedule is the rest of the week as we try to get Perry on site as quickly as possible,<br>I will follow up the moment we are out of the shop along with the police scheduling.""<br><br>12/22:  Per Trucking/Delivery Company, Pod 53075 is broke down in TX currently. We thought he would be fixed by now but is waiting on a part now.  New Delivery Date to be 12/20/2025.</P><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-30 08:25: Per Trucking/Delivery Company: This POD is now tentatively set to be delivered on 1/2/2026.<br>Updates/History:<br>12/30: Truck broke down/in shop for repair. (details below)<br>Per Trucking/Delivery Company Our driver Perry is experiencing a D-Rating issue with the truck this am and does not have power. He is currently in a shop, but this will not allow us to meet our police this am to get on site this afternoon. I truly apologize for this! The goal is to get out of the shop today and we are working on police scheduling for tomorrow. I am curious what the sites schedule is the rest of the week as we try to get Perry on site as quickly as possible,<br>I will follow up the moment we are out of the shop along with the police scheduling.""<br><br>12/22: Per Trucking/Delivery Company, Pod 53075 is broke down in TX</P></BODY></HTML>
%R	2730071	83219400	106343	237851	<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN""><HTML><HEAD><META content=""text/html; charset=unicode""http-equiv=Content-Type><META name=HENERATOR content=""MSHTML 11.00.10570.1011""></HEAD><BODY><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-02 12:37: Fibrebond Delivery date is 12/22. Due to the coordination and/or the other building ROJ dates impacting DC1 ROJs, this has been pushed out. Fibrebond can only deliver so many a week and all building need by dates overlap.</P></BODY></HTML>
