%R	2730088	83229903	106343	237851	<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN""><HTML><HEAD><META content=""text/html; charset=unicode""http-equiv=Content-Type><META name=HENERATOR content=""MSHTML 11.00.10570.1011""></HEAD><BODY><P>John Capriotti on 2025-12-30 08:30: Pending delivery of last zone 2 POD (UPS Container #F12): ETA now 1/2/2026 (details below)<br>Per Trucking/Delivery Company: This POD is now tentatively set to be delivered on 1/2/2026.<br>Updates/History:<br>12/30: Truck broke down/in shop for repair. (details below)<br>Per Trucking/Delivery Company Our driver Perry is experiencing a D-Rating issue with the truck this am and does not have power. He is currently in a shop, but this will not allow us to meet our police this am to get on site this afternoon. I truly apologize for this! The goal is to get out of the shop today and we are working on police scheduling for tomorrow. I am curious what the sites schedule is the rest of the week as we try to get Perry on site as quickly as possible,<br>I will follow up the moment we are out of the shop along with the police scheduling.""<br><br>12/22: Per Trucking/Delivery Company, Pod 53075 is broke down in TX</P></BODY></HTML>
%R	2730089	83222745	106343	237851	<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN""><HTML><HEAD><META content=""text/html; charset=unicode""http-equiv=Content-Type><META name=HENERATOR content=""MSHTML 11.00.10570.1011""></HEAD><BODY><P>Jack Garrett on 2025-10-21 08:10: correct start date</P><P>Jack Garrett on 2025-10-21 08:10: correct projected delivery date.</P><P>Jack Garrett on 2025-12-02 12:01: Case work pushed back and being stored off site.</P></BODY></HTML>
